<title>PHILIPPINES: RFM tuna project gets tax incentives.</title>
<headline>RFM tuna project gets tax incentives.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' Board of Investments (BOI) said on Monday it had approved the 30 million peso expansion plan of RFM Corp's canned tuna venture.</p>
<p>The project will be eligible for tax and tariff incentives, the BOI said.</p>
<p>RFM Corp, one of the country's biggest food and beverage companies, planned to expand its tuna canning line by 87 percent to 940,604 cases every year. The expanded capacity will be on stream by July this year.</p>
<p>The canned tuna will be exported to the United States, Canada, and Europe.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
